{offset200}{ia13}{arial}
{offset0}Operator: {arialbld}Chief Barkod{arial}

{offset25}{micro}Graduate Chemist from Camford{arial}




{offset0}from: Sergeï Sakharin

to: {rank} {name}





The Allied High Strategic Command has put its trust in my experience for co-ordinating this campaign.

The new tank at the Tektons' disposal is terrifyingly powerful, but I'm afraid we haven't seen the last Psycho inventions of death.

Reports from aerial observation indicate great activity on Ratmüde Island, flak batteries have been identified but also some strange installations. 
They look like ramps for ski-jumping. Our analysts have proposed numerous hypotheses on the use of these ramps, we think they're used as launching pads for a kind of rocket-plane. This version seems to have been confirmed by numerous witnesses who observed the flight of a small aircraft without propellers passing through at high speed. Seen from the coast of Legoland only a few miles away from Ratmüde Island, the witnesses swear they had never seen such an aircraft before.

Our advance into Polnakia has allowed us to make a sharp breach into the heart of Tektonia, dividing the enemy front in two. Tankred's navy at {arialbld}Wizmar{arial} in the north is now cut off from Otton's tanks in the south at {arialbld}Blizna.{arial} We also know that Karlo has been sent to {arialbld}Ratmüde{arial} with a mission to seal off all of its airspace.

We will push within this breach so as to further isolate Otton and Tankred and prevent them from causing harm. Once done we can rally for storming on Ratmüde.

This will be our marching order:

My division of the Katzars' Dragons, will be in the north-west at {arialbld}Rostok{arial}. I'll take care of sawing up Tankred's crutches.

Markus and his Psycho rebels will be on the south-east coast at {arialbld}Wroklaw{arial}, ready to give Otton's skull a close shave.

As for you {name}, you will be in the center of this plan at {arialbld}Proznak{arial}, you must sustain us in our respective actions. If you give back any ground to the Tektons, we'll all be dead.


{offset100}Sergeï Sakharin

{offset150}Commodore General, of the New Katzarin Republics.



{offset200}{signature5}{offset0}



